<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Maria Capua Vetere</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Maria Capua Vetere is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the site of ancient Capua, once the largest city of southern Italy. Its remains include a great Roman amphitheatre, second in size only to the Colosseum, and a painted Mithraeum. The gladiator revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartacus">Spartacus</a> began in a training school there in 73 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-maria-capua-vetere.jpg" alt="Santa Maria Capua Vetere" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dom De Felice e Carla Nunziata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Amphitheatre_of_Santa_Maria_Capua_Vetere_004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
